==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|cocur}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|gmw|ang}} {{m|gem-pro||*kokar-}}, whence also Old Frisian ''[[koker]]'', Old Saxon ''kokar'' (Dutch ''[[koker]]''), Old High German ''[[kohhar|kohhār]]'' (German ''[[Köcher]]''). The origin of the West Germanic word is unknown, but note that a similar word can be found in Turkic and Mongolic languages: see {{cog|xgn-pro|*kökexür}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkoker/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# a [[quiver]] for arrows
# a [[case]], [[container]]
# a [[sheath]]

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|coker}}, {{l|enm|cokre}}
** English: {{l|en|cogger}}, {{l|en|scogger}}
*** Scots: {{l|sco|scogger}}

