==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|coquere}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|coquō}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|es}} {{m|ine-pro|*pekʷ-||to cook, become ripe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Castilian}} {{IPA|/ko.ˈθer/|lang=es}}
* {{a|Latin America}} {{IPA|/ko.ˈser/|lang=es}}
* {{homophones|coser|lang=es}} (''non-Castilian dialects'')

===Verb===
{{es-verb|coc|er|pres=cuezo}}

# to [[boil]]
#: ''cocer a fuego lento'' - [[simmer]]
# {{lb|es|reflexive|cocerse}} to [[brew]]
#: ''Algo se está '''cociendo'''''
# {{lb|es|pronominal}} to [[chafe]] {{gloss|get sore}}

